2. Define the dynamic configuration rules
These are the rules the rebuilt backend must implement.
Area	Required behaviour
Branch	A registered community/branch owns its configurations.
Configuration	An admin can create multiple distinct configurations under one branch.
Contribution	Amount is defined per configuration.
Frequency	One frequency per configuration: weekly or monthly.
Capacity	Maximum co-savers is defined per configuration, not globally.
Collection positions	Defined by the configuration; for one payout per co-saver, the number of positions must match the number of co-savers.
Duration	Derived from the configuration's frequency and collection positions.
Immutability	A configuration's terms cannot be edited after creation. Changed terms require a new configuration.
Tenant	Each tenant belongs to exactly one configuration and one branch.
Tenant sequence	Each configuration has its own independent sequence of tenants.
Activation	A tenant activates only when its capacity is filled and every member is onboarded and verified.
Schedule	Contribution and payout schedules start from the actual activation date.
Next tenant	When a tenant fills, the next tenant is generated under the same configuration.
A configuration must remain distinct even when another configuration under the same branch has identical-looking terms, unless the product explicitly decides to prevent duplicate configurations.
