Phase E — Rebuild payout and TVC logic
TVC is a position-based adjustment capped at 50% of one single contribution amount.
•	It is calculated using the co-saver's collection position (slot).
•	The maximum adjustment is 50% of one contribution.
•	It is not a percentage of the gross savings pool.
•	It must derive dynamically from the configured contribution amount and collection positions.
For example, if the contribution is £100, the maximum TVC adjustment is £50.
Task 20. Implement dynamic payout positions
•	Every collection position must come from the group's configuration.
•	Payout order must cover the configured positions.
•	Every eligible member receives the correct position.
•	No payout position may be duplicated.
•	Payout progression must stop at the configured final position.
Task 21. Rebuild the TVC calculation
TVC mean time value contribution percentage adjustment derived from the contribution amount. It is 50% of a single contribution amount. It is a fixed proportional deduction of the configured per-member contribution. The calculation must use the actual configured number of positions and the member's actual collection position. 
an example using a £100 contribution and 5 co-savers, with the TVC adjustment capped at 50% of one contribution (£50).
Collection position	TVC adjustment
1st	-£50
2nd	-£25
3rd	£0
4th	+£25
5th	+£50
The adjustments total zero.
What this means:
•	The first co-saver receives £50 less than the gross pool.
•	The second receives £25 less.
•	The third receives the gross pool.
•	The fourth receives £25 more.
•	The fifth receives £50 more.
If the contribution is £200, the maximum adjustment becomes £100.
The key principle: TVC scales with the contribution amount. The maximum adjustment is always 50% of one contribution, not 50% of the total pool.
The implementation must use precise monetary arithmetic and define how the derived rate is converted into the relevant cycle rate. It must also test rounding and positive/negative adjustments across odd and even circle sizes.
